# Design Style: Material Design 3 (Material You)

Expressive, accessible, adaptive UI built on color roles, tonal surfaces, a shape scale, and a fixed type scale. Always use semantic role tokens, never raw hex values, in components.

## Principles
1. Color is role-based: every color has a purpose (primary, secondary, tertiary, surface, error) and a paired "on-" color for content placed on it.
2. Elevation is mostly tonal: higher surfaces get a tinted surface-container color; shadows are subtle and secondary.
3. Shapes are rounded and use a defined scale. Don't invent radii.
4. Interaction feedback uses state layers (translucent overlays), not color swaps.
5. Layouts adapt across window size classes (compact / medium / expanded).
6. Motion is purposeful, with emphasized easing for large transitions.

## Color tokens (baseline palette; regenerate from a brand seed color with Material Theme Builder, then replace these values)
