```
Usage: page background = `surface`; cards/sheets = `surface-container*`; text on surface = `on-surface`; secondary text = `on-surface-variant`; borders = `outline` / `outline-variant`. Use `primary` for the single most important action, `secondary-container` for tonal/less prominent controls, `tertiary` for accents. Support dynamic color via a seed when the user asks for theming.

## Typography (Roboto, or a system sans fallback; size / line-height px, weight)
| Role | Size/LH | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| Display L / M / S | 57/64, 45/52, 36/44 | 400 |
| Headline L / M / S | 32/40, 28/36, 24/32 | 400 |
| Title L | 22/28 | 400 |
| Title M / S | 16/24, 14/20 | 500 |
| Body L / M / S | 16/24, 14/20, 12/16 | 400 |
| Label L / M / S | 14/20, 12/16, 11/16 | 500 |

Define these as classes/tokens (e.g. `.md-title-medium`) and use them instead of ad hoc sizes. Sentence case for labels and buttons, not ALL CAPS.

## Shape scale
```css
:root {
  --md-shape-none: 0;  --md-shape-xs: 4px;  --md-shape-sm: 8px;
  --md-shape-md: 12px; --md-shape-lg: 16px; --md-shape-xl: 28px; --md-shape-full: 9999px;
}
```
Buttons/chips/FAB-extended/search = full or sm per component; cards = md; dialogs/sheets = xl; text fields = xs (top corners when filled).

## Elevation
- Level 0: surface. Level 1: cards (`surface-container-low`). Level 2: menus, nav bar (`surface-container`). Level 3: FAB, dialogs, search (`surface-container-high`). Prefer tonal color; add only soft shadows, e.g. `0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.15)` for level 1-2.

## State layers
Overlay the content color on the container: hover 8%, focus 10%, pressed 10%, dragged 16%. Disabled: content 38% opacity, container 12%. Implement with a `::before` pseudo-element using `currentColor` or `--md-on-surface` and the opacity above.

## Components
- **Buttons:** Filled (primary, highest emphasis), Filled tonal (secondary-container), Outlined (1px `outline`), Text (no container), Elevated. Height 40px, full radius, 24px horizontal padding, Label Large. One filled button per view area.
- **FAB:** 56px, `primary-container` / `on-primary-container`, radius `lg` (16px), level 3. Extended FAB includes a label.
- **Cards:** Elevated (`surface-container-low`), Filled (`surface-container-highest`), Outlined (1px `outline-variant`). Radius `md`, 16px padding.
- **Text fields:** Filled (default; `surface-container-highest`, bottom indicator) or Outlined; floating label; error uses `error` for label, indicator, and supporting text.
- **Navigation:** Compact = bottom navigation bar (3-5 destinations, active = `secondary-container` pill indicator); Medium = navigation rail; Expanded = navigation drawer. Top app bar: small/center-aligned, or large collapsing for hero screens.
- **Chips, switches, checkboxes, sliders, dialogs, snackbars, tabs, menus:** follow standard M3 patterns (pill indicators, 52x32 switch, dialogs with `surface-container-high` at `xl` radius and a scrim at 32% opacity).
- **Icons:** Material Symbols (Rounded or Outlined), 24px, optical size matched, filled style for the active state.
- **Lists:** 56-72px rows, leading icon/avatar, headline + supporting text, dividers via `outline-variant` only when needed.

## Layout and adaptivity
- Window size classes: Compact < 600px (1 pane, bottom nav, 16px margins), Medium 600-839px (rail, 24px margins), Expanded >= 840px (drawer or rail, multi-pane/list-detail, 24px margins).
- 4-column grid on compact, 8 on medium, 12 on expanded. Spacing in multiples of 4px (8 / 16 / 24 are most common).
- Minimum touch target 48x48px.

## Motion
```css
:root {
  --md-ease-standard: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  --md-ease-emphasized-decelerate: cubic-bezier(0.05, 0.7, 0.1, 1);
  --md-ease-emphasized-accelerate: cubic-bezier(0.3, 0, 0.8, 0.15);
  --md-dur-short: 150ms; --md-dur-medium: 300ms; --md-dur-long: 500ms;
}
```
Small state changes 100-200ms standard easing; entering elements use emphasized-decelerate, exiting use emphasized-accelerate (about 200-400ms); shared-axis / container-transform patterns for navigation. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Accessibility
- Pairings of role + on-role colors are designed for >= 4.5:1 contrast; preserve them when customizing and verify custom seeds.
- Visible focus indicator (state layer plus 3px outline in `secondary`/`primary` offset 2px for keyboard focus). Don't rely on color alone for error or selected states.

## Implementation notes
- Prefer the official `@material/web` components (`md-filled-button`, etc.) or Material UI (MUI v6+ with an M3 theme) when the stack allows; otherwise implement with the tokens above.
- Tailwind: map tokens in `theme.extend.colors` (e.g. `primary: 'var(--md-primary)'`) so classes like `bg-primary text-on-primary` work.

## Don't
- Don't hardcode hex values or arbitrary radii/font sizes in components; use tokens.
- Don't use pure-black shadows for depth in place of tonal surface colors.
- Don't use ALL CAPS buttons (that's Material 2), sharp corners, or more than one filled primary button competing in the same area.
- Don't mix M2 patterns (raised buttons, elevation-by-shadow, bottom app bar with cradle) into M3 screens.
